{#
    The purchase side's product field: core's shared partial, pointed at THIS bundle's search
    endpoint so the results carry what the vendor charges us.

    The field itself moved to `admin/_partials/product_field.html.twig` when Inventory Depth needed
    the same three tiers (#8) — core being the only layer neither bundle can delete. This file
    stays, and stays callable under `@Procurement/_product_field.html.twig` with exactly the
    parameters it always took, because six screens include it and more are being written; a rename
    would break whichever of them is on a branch right now.

    Parameters: as core's, minus `searchUrl`, plus —

    vendorId      optional  scopes the search results' cost to this vendor's rate card

    Everything else — field, products, remote, selected, form, required, label — is passed straight
    through. `only` is deliberate: this partial is included from templates that leak their whole
    context, and forwarding that context would let a stray `searchUrl` in a caller quietly point a
    purchase screen's field at a different endpoint.
#}
{{ include('admin/_partials/product_field.html.twig', {
    field: field,
    products: products,
    remote: remote,
    selected: selected is defined ? selected : null,
    form: form is defined ? form : null,
    required: required|default(false),
    label: label|default('Product'),
    placeholder: placeholder is defined ? placeholder : null,
    searchUrl: path('admin_bundle_procurement_product_search') ~ (vendorId is defined and vendorId ? '?vendor_id=' ~ vendorId : ''),
}, with_context = false) }}
